    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Logistic-SuSiE approximations along the set-size axis: full grid\"\nsubtitle: \"CAVI-Q2 vs gIBSS-Q2 vs gIBSS-Laplace vs global-JJ vs score (experiment 022, n=1000, L=5, 200 reps)\"\nengine: jupyter\njupyter: python3\nexecute:\n  fig-dpi: 110\n---\n\n\nFive logistic-SuSiE arms, all in the Gaussian family $\\mathcal{Q}_2$ (see the\n[pilot](results.qmd) for the arm definitions). Design: sparse 0/1 columns ($n = 1000$,\n$p = 256$, adjacent-column $\\phi = 0.8$), $b_0 = -2$, $L^* = 3$ causals at gap 8 (binary\n$\\phi \\approx 0.47$ between causals) or 64 ($\\phi \\approx 0.05$), fit with $L = 5$. Axis:\nexpected set size $m$, with $\\beta$ calibrated per $m$ to $E[\\text{LRT}] = T$ so detectability\nis matched and only the shape of each feature's likelihood changes with $m$.\n\nAll CS metrics are over **declared** CSs (component $\\log \\text{BF} \\ge 2$). An undeclared\ncomponent has $\\alpha$ near uniform and a 95% set of ~240 of 256 features, so its coverage is\n1 by construction; pooling it in would erase every difference. The ranking of the arms is the\nsame at every $\\log \\text{BF}$ cut from 0 to 10.\n\n::: {#status .cell execution_count=2}\n022-laplace: 24 signal cells x 5 arms, 200-200 reps per cell; 6 null cells.\n:::\n\n\n# Headline: pooled over m {#sec-pooled}\n\n::: {#tab-pooled .cell execution_count=3}\nCAVI-Q2 in absolute terms; every other arm as **arm minus CAVI-Q2** on the same replicates. *coverage*: fraction of declared CSs containing a causal. *size*: median declared-CS size with its interquartile range. *power*: mean over reps of the fraction of the 3 causals captured by a declared CS. *CS/fit*: declared CSs per fit. 95% CIs resample replicates (the independent unit; CSs within a fit are not), jointly for both arms of a difference.\n\n| T | gap | arm | coverage [95% CI] | size (IQR) | power [95% CI] | CS/fit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | 8 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.898 [0.881, 0.914] | 4 (2-7) | 0.448 [0.431, 0.465] | 1.05 |\n| 8 | 8 | gIBSS-Q2 - CAVI-Q2 | +0.009 [+0.004, +0.015] | 4 (2-7) | +0.011 [+0.004, +0.018] | 1.06 |\n| 8 | 8 | gIBSS-Laplace - CAVI-Q2 | +0.015 [+0.008, +0.022] | 4 (2-7) | +0.012 [+0.004, +0.020] | 1.04 |\n| 8 | 8 | global-JJ - CAVI-Q2 | -0.090 [-0.109, -0.071] | 2 (1-5) | -0.092 [-0.106, -0.078] | 1.06 |\n| 8 | 8 | score - CAVI-Q2 | -0.055 [-0.071, -0.041] | 3 (2-5) | +0.001 [-0.016, +0.018] | 1.24 |\n| 8 | 64 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.918 [0.894, 0.942] | 7 (3-17) | 0.161 [0.147, 0.175] | 0.43 |\n| 8 | 64 | gIBSS-Q2 - CAVI-Q2 | -0.004 [-0.011, +0.003] | 7 (3-17) | -0.002 [-0.009, +0.005] | 0.42 |\n| 8 | 64 | gIBSS-Laplace - CAVI-Q2 | +0.010 [-0.000, +0.020] | 7 (3-19) | -0.004 [-0.012, +0.003] | 0.40 |\n| 8 | 64 | global-JJ - CAVI-Q2 | -0.092 [-0.119, -0.064] | 4 (2-8) | -0.025 [-0.036, -0.013] | 0.45 |\n| 8 | 64 | score - CAVI-Q2 | -0.099 [-0.124, -0.074] | 5 (2-11) | +0.104 [+0.087, +0.121] | 0.84 |\n| 16 | 8 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.946 [0.936, 0.956] | 2 (1-4) | 0.632 [0.616, 0.647] | 1.62 |\n| 16 | 8 | gIBSS-Q2 - CAVI-Q2 | +0.004 [+0.000, +0.008] | 2 (1-5) | +0.002 [-0.004, +0.007] | 1.60 |\n| 16 | 8 | gIBSS-Laplace - CAVI-Q2 | +0.008 [+0.004, +0.013] | 2 (1-5) | +0.008 [+0.001, +0.015] | 1.60 |\n| 16 | 8 | global-JJ - CAVI-Q2 | -0.039 [-0.050, -0.029] | 2 (1-3) | -0.066 [-0.079, -0.055] | 1.61 |\n| 16 | 8 | score - CAVI-Q2 | -0.040 [-0.050, -0.030] | 2 (1-4) | -0.026 [-0.040, -0.012] | 1.72 |\n| 16 | 64 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.960 [0.951, 0.969] | 3 (2-7) | 0.531 [0.514, 0.549] | 1.53 |\n| 16 | 64 | gIBSS-Q2 - CAVI-Q2 | -0.001 [-0.004, +0.002] | 3 (2-8) | -0.008 [-0.017, +0.001] | 1.50 |\n| 16 | 64 | gIBSS-Laplace - CAVI-Q2 | +0.003 [+0.000, +0.006] | 3 (2-8) | -0.015 [-0.024, -0.006] | 1.48 |\n| 16 | 64 | global-JJ - CAVI-Q2 | -0.034 [-0.044, -0.025] | 2 (1-4) | -0.024 [-0.038, -0.011] | 1.58 |\n| 16 | 64 | score - CAVI-Q2 | -0.046 [-0.056, -0.036] | 3 (1-5) | +0.082 [+0.066, +0.098] | 1.93 |\n:::\n\n\n# Along m {#sec-along-m}\n\n## Relative to CAVI-Q2 {#sec-delta}\n\n::: {#cell-fi